In 2019, a 27-year-old student pulled off one of the boldest food scams ever. He walked into KFC outlets claiming he was a food inspector sent from the KFC headquarters for a food quality check to taste if they're up to standard. But he got caught when KFC's actual food inspector came into the same restaurant he just left. And when KFC caught news of this, they set up a trap on their other outlets to catch him in the act. Eventually, it worked and he got arrested by the police. 
